---@class vercel.connect.ConnectConnectorCreateResult
---@field accentColor? string Hex accent color (e.g., `#000000`) for branding.
---@field appTokens? vercel.connect.ConnectConnectorCreateResultAppTokens App-token capabilities and known grants for the connector.
---@field backgroundColor? string Hex background color (e.g., `#000000`) for branding.
---@field clientUrl? string|distilled.Null Provider-side URL for viewing or managing the resource represented by the connector. The destination can be an app, account, phone line, or service instance, depending on the connector type.
---@field connectionMethod? string The connection method this connector was created from, when the create request named one.
---@field createdAt number Creation time in epoch milliseconds.
---@field createdBy? vercel.connect.ConnectConnectorCreateResultCreatedBy Principal that created the connector.
---@field creationMode? vercel.connect.ConnectConnectorCreateResultCreationMode How the connector row was originally created. New create paths stamp this explicitly; older rows may omit it.
---@field defaultInstallationId? string Installation used when a token request does not specify an installation.
---@field devsite? string Developer website for the connected service.
---@field displayName string Human-readable connector name.
---@field docsite? string Developer documentation for the connected service.
---@field events? vercel.connect.ConnectConnectorCreateResultEventsList Known events this connector subscribes to (e.g. Slack bot events, GitHub webhook events). Names are type-specific and validated by the managed-create flow when forwarded to the third-party service.
---@field hasMcpEventDeliveries? boolean Whether Connect has successfully delivered an MCP event for this connector.
---@field icon? string Connector branding icon. SHA-1 hash that resolves to the uploaded icon through the Vercel avatar service. Consumers render this with `https://vercel.com/api/www/avatar/{icon}`.
---@field id string Stable `scl_` connector ID. Use this value directly in `{connector}`.
---@field knownStale? boolean Whether the connector is known to have been edited since the app package it publishes to the provider was last built, so that package no longer matches it. Absent when it was not computed, or when the connector type publishes no such package. Derived on every read rather than marked at edit time, so reverting an edit clears it. Only reported by connector types that publish a package a user has to re-publish by hand — Microsoft Teams today.
---@field managed? vercel.connect.ConnectConnectorCreateResultManaged Managed connector metadata exposed without leaking the manager connector or installation identifiers.
---@field mcpEventsUiVisibility? vercel.connect.ConnectConnectorCreateResultMcpEventsUiVisibility MCP Events dashboard visibility. Defaults to auto: show after the first successful delivery.
---@field name string Connector name within the owning team.
---@field redirectUri? string Redirect URI registered with the third-party service for this connector, if any. Used by `startAuthorization`/`startInstallation` to replay the exact URI back to the provider's token endpoint. Absent on connectors created before this field was introduced; those callers fall back to the `https://connect.vercel.com/callback` default.
---@field reinstallAt? number Time when this connector started requiring reinstallation because an installation-affecting app-token grant changed.
---@field service string Best-effort identifier of the third-party service this connector represents, independent of `type`. Examples: `'slack'`, `'mcp.linear.app'`, and `'auth.example.com'`. Always present in API responses.
---@field serviceIcon? string Provider logo from the known-service registry, matched by `service`. Often an SVG data URL. Absent when the service is not in the registry.
---@field supportedSubjectTypes vercel.connect.ConnectConnectorCreateResultSupportedSubjectTypesList Token subject types supported by the connector.
---@field supportsIcon any Whether the connector icon can propagate to the provider.
---@field supportsInstallation boolean Whether the connector supports an installation flow.
---@field supportsManagedEjection? boolean Whether this managed connector can disconnect from its manager.
---@field supportsRevocation boolean Whether Connect can revoke tokens for this connector.
---@field supportsTriggers boolean Whether this connector type supports trigger webhooks. Derived from the type definition; indicates that `triggers` and `triggerDestinations` may be meaningful for this connector.
---@field target? string Which of the service's products/surfaces this connector points at.
---@field triggerDestinations? vercel.connect.ConnectConnectorCreateResultTriggerDestinationsList Destinations that incoming triggers should be forwarded to. Limited to 3 entries. Set the initial destination with `triggerDestination` during creation. Replace the complete set with `PATCH /v1/connect/connectors/{connector}/trigger-destinations`. Computed routing environments are stored internally, not returned here.
---@field triggers? vercel.connect.ConnectTriggerConfiguration Incoming trigger configuration for the connector.
---@field type vercel.connect.ConnectConnectorCreateResultType Connector implementation type.
---@field typeIcon? string Icon identifier supplied by the connector type.
---@field typeName string Human-readable name of the connector type.
---@field uid string Team-scoped UID. URL-encode this value before using it in `{connector}`.
---@field updatedAt number Last update time in epoch milliseconds.
---@field updatedBy? vercel.connect.ConnectConnectorCreateResultUpdatedBy Principal that most recently updated the connector.
---@field userTokens? vercel.connect.ConnectConnectorCreateResultUserTokens User-token capabilities and known grants for the connector.
---@field website? string Public website for the connected service.

---App-token capabilities and known grants for the connector.
